  "name": "mall_weekend",
  "title": "Weekend mall shop: afternoon and evening family peaks, group orders",
  "provenance": {
    "source": "Synthetic, anchored on the Course 5006 parameter set and on teaching-case ranges for shopping-centre weekend traffic",
    "method": "Piecewise-constant demand with a slow opening, afternoon peak, dinner dip and evening peak; daily mean normalised to the quoted rate; batch arrivals model families and friend groups; four baristas and three tea slots so the evening peak is tight but finite",
    "uncertainty": "high",
    "notes": "Not field-measured. Twelve-hour modelled day (720 min). Group orders (20% of arrivals, mean 2.5 people) are the main reason the peak rate exceeds the daily mean on a per-person basis. Two ice slots represent a larger mall counter."
  },
